# defconfig for Honor Play (COR-AL00) with Kirin 970 (Hi3670)
# Based on arm64 defconfig with Kirin 970 specific options
#
# Every CONFIG_ symbol below has been verified against linux-7.2.5 Kconfig
# (checked 2026-09-20).
#
# Dead symbols REMOVED (kconfig ignores unknown symbols silently, so they
# looked enabled but never were):
#   MMC_DW_HI3XXX   -> MMC_DW_K3      (dw_mmc-k3.c matches hisilicon,hi3660-dw-mshc)
#   SP805_WDT       -> ARM_SP805_WATCHDOG + WATCHDOG_CORE
#   RESET_HISI_HI6460, SCSI_UFS_DWC_TEGRA_D, BATTERY_GENERIC, DRM_DW,
#   QCOM_QFPROM
# Removed as no longer existing upstream:
#   USELIB, ARCH_RODATA_DEFAULT_ENABLE, ARM64_SSBD, ARM64_ERRATUM_1542435,
#   NTP_SYSCALLS, HARDEN_BRANCH_PREDICTOR (ARM-only), HISI_PMU (needs ACPI;
#   this board is DT-only), CRYPTO_SHA1/2_ARM64_CE + CRYPTO_AES_ARM64_CE
#   (renamed to CRYPTO_AES_ARM64_CE_BLK / CRYPTO_GHASH_ARM64_CE).
#
# PCIE_KIRIN still exists; it moved to drivers/pci/controller/dwc/Kconfig.
#
# hisi_dpe/Kconfig was also fixed: DRM_HISI_DPE now selects
# DRM_CLIENT_SELECTION (else DRM_FBDEV_EMULATION never applies) and
# DRM_HISI_DSI now selects DRM_MIPI_DSI + DRM_PANEL_BRIDGE (else the panel
# drivers fail to link with undefined mipi_dsi_* references).
#

